WEBVTT

00:00:02.822 --> 00:00:05.995
The factory reviews every pull request, including mine.

00:00:05.995 --> 00:00:12.342
On this one it found a critical bug: a dry run of the log scan would still have closed real tickets in Linear.

00:00:14.023 --> 00:00:16.873
It was right, and I fixed it before it merged.

00:00:16.873 --> 00:00:19.103
So far, that's ordinary code review.

00:00:21.648 --> 00:00:27.328
When a pull request closes, the factory reads the whole review and asks whether there is a lesson worth keeping.

00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:33.768
Here there was, so it opened this pull request against the instructions every agent reads in this repository, in its own words.

00:00:36.606 --> 00:00:39.719
It says what it learned and links the review it came from.

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:45.246
It goes through the same checks as code, and guidance pull requests like this one now merge themselves.

00:00:49.023 --> 00:00:55.663
The same lesson is in agent-setup, the instructions every agent session loads on my machines, before it writes a line.

00:00:59.146 --> 00:01:01.589
It keeps doing it: thirty four lessons so far.

00:01:01.589 --> 00:01:03.235
The newest merged this evening.

00:01:03.235 --> 00:01:09.660
A review caught a change that could lower a dependency's version, so now the vulnerability fix instructions say never to.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.226
Each one is a mistake caught once and written down, so the agents don't make it again.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:20.274
That was the learning loop: review comments that turn into rules the agents follow.

00:01:20.274 --> 00:01:25.414
Most of what code review teaches is lost when the pull request merges, and here it's kept.
